    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>360\u00b0 Panorama Viewer</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Imagine a virtual journey where you can explore stunning 360-degree panoramas as if you were actually there. Revisit your memories by viewing your own panoramic shots and reliving moments you once experienced.</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Free camera control:</strong> You can rotate the camera in any direction, zoom in and out on areas of interest, and take 8K snapshots.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Automatic demonstration mode:</strong> If you release the mouse and keys for 5 seconds, the program will automatically start showing panoramas. It smoothly rotates the image horizontally by 400 degrees, then the panorama fades out and the next one appears.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Easy start:</strong> To begin, simply select a folder with spherical panoramic photos and click the &quot;View Photos&quot; button.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The 360\u00b0 panorama viewer is perfect for users with extensive collections of spherical 360-degree panoramas and owners of cameras for their shooting. The quality of snapshots taken by pressing the &quot;S&quot; key directly depends on the quality of the panoramas themselves.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The program supports .jpg and .png files.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
